{
  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "version": 1,
  "game": "kpb105",
  "notes": "Capcom Kingpin C1.04 Lamp Test walk on fresh isolated state. Each flipper step selects one lamp; the DMD names it (for example 11A - COIN 1/COIN 3) with its column/row drivers, connector pins and wire colours, and the public lamp that turns on in that step pairs the ROM lamp name with the public lamp address. The walk runs forward with the right flipper and then backward with the left flipper; each pass covers every position, so the second is an independent cross-check. Retain the DMD frames to prove the path taken. Flipper buttons are pressed through PinMAME's flipper-column button bits (public 84 left, 82 right): kpb105 declares FLIP_SWNO(5,6), and with keyboard handling off core_updateSw copies those bits into matrix switches 5/6 every frame, so a direct host write to 5 or 6 lasts at most one frame.",
